Description: composite: don't copy to or from a rootless server's root.
 When a window is redirected, compNewPixmap seeds its new pixmap with what
 is under it in the parent, and compRestoreWindow copies it back on
 unredirect. A rootless server's root has no image: its pixmap is one
 scanline that every row aliases (devKind 0). fb reads that harmlessly,
 but glamor's CopyArea uploads it as a full-size image and reads far past
 the allocation. Xnextbsd on the GPU segfaulted in v3d_move_tiled_image
 as soon as Chromium's screen-share picker redirected the top-level
 windows for its thumbnails. Skip both copies when the parent is a root
 with a zero-stride pixmap; there is nothing there to copy.
Origin: NextBSD
 (nextbsd/apps-xlibre#34, E37 nextbsd/nextbsd#625)
Forwarded: not-needed (NextBSD only, for now)
---
--- a/composite/compalloc.c
+++ b/composite/compalloc.c
@@ -230,13 +230,30 @@
     return status;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A rootless server's root has no image: its pixmap is one scanline that
+ * every row aliases (devKind 0). There is nothing to copy to or from it,
+ * and an accelerated CopyArea or Composite (glamor) would treat it as a
+ * full-size image and run past its end.
+ */
+static Bool
+compRootlessRoot(WindowPtr pWin)
+{
+    ScreenPtr pScreen = pWin->drawable.pScreen;
+
+    return pWin->parent == NULL &&
+        (*pScreen->GetWindowPixmap) (pWin)->devKind == 0;
+}
+
